course: dictionary
lesson: 550
title: Attention: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Attention is a noun, and it has more than one meaning. It can mean listening, watching or thinking carefully. It can mean the interest or notice that people give you. It can also mean care, as in medical attention.
explain: «Hunger shows as a rumbling tummy, low energy, grumpiness and trouble paying attention.» The clues are rumbling tummy and low energy, and the sentence is about being hungry. So attention here means focusing on what you are doing.
explain: «Scary predictions online are usually nonsense meant to get attention.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try "notice" in place of attention. It still makes sense, so this attention means the interest or notice that people give you.
explain: «Distraction... helps the brain pay less attention to pain.» Here attention means focus, and the context is pain. When you meet a word with many meanings, test each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that fits.
fact: Attention is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say "a lot of attention", not "two attentions".
fact: Attention means listening, watching or thinking carefully about something, as in «pay attention».
fact: Attention can mean the interest or notice people give you, as in «A headline... grabs attention».
fact: Attention can mean care, as in «medical attention», which is a doctor's care.
fact: Your attention span is how long you can focus on one thing, and memory games train it.
exercise: In school, a teacher says «Attention, please!» What does it mean? | *Everyone, listen to me now | Everyone, sing a song | Everyone, put your bags away | Everyone, go outside now
exercise: «A headline is the title of a news story; it is short, bold and grabs attention.» What does attention mean here? | *Interest or notice from readers | Care from a doctor | A quiet room | Standing up straight
exercise: «Hunger shows as... trouble paying attention.» What does «trouble paying attention» mean? | Being very loud and noisy | *Trouble focusing on what you are doing | Trouble with a doctor | Trouble getting to school on time
test: What does «medical attention» mean? | A loud bell | A medal for sport | *A doctor's care | A new book
test: «Distraction... helps the brain pay less attention to pain.» What does attention mean in this sentence? | Being noticed by a crowd | Standing still in a line | Medical care | *Focus on something
exam: «Scary predictions online are usually nonsense meant to get attention.» Which meaning of attention fits? | Standing straight like a soldier | Care from a doctor | *Interest or notice from people | Listening carefully in class
